From fa8d2301637de9cf37bca33836660d01ace2ec2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 00:44:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 702/702] SableOS: Phone contacts list with A-Z rail, letter
 keys and numbers

Ports the approved SableOS Phone presentation to the LineageOS Dialer
contacts tab:

* One alphabet rail: an A-Z rail at the end edge reads the adapter's
  existing address-book index; letters without contacts are dimmed and
  skipped by focus, and while it shows the upstream scroll thumb is
  hidden so there is a single rail.
* Physical keyboard: on the contacts tab a letter key (no Ctrl, Alt or
  Meta, not held) moves focus to the first contact under that letter
  and repeating it cycles; with no match focus stays and "No contacts
  under X" is shown. Letters never open or call anyone. Keys reach the
  list only when no view handled them, so text fields keep them.
* Each row shows the contact's default number and its type under the
  name, from one read-only ContactsProvider Phone query reduced off the
  main thread into the bounded SablePreferredNumbers map. It reloads on
  provider changes and writes nothing.
* The bottom navigation bar is flat (no elevation). Colours keep
  following the system palette, which the Sable accent drives.

ContactsProvider stays the owner of contact data; accounts, sync,
permissions and contact semantics are unchanged. Telephony, dialpad,
in-call and Call/End key behaviour are untouched.
